OL,3,AWoman with Ebola in Nigeria confirmed
OL,4,Aas wife of Swiss diplomat
OL,5,
OL,6,FSwitzerland's foreign ministry has
OL,7,Fconfirmed that the woman who has tested
OL,8,Fpositive for Ebola in Nigeria is the
OL,9,Fwife of a Swiss diplomat.
OL,11,FThe woman, a 42-year-old Ugandan-born
OL,12,Fnational who lives in the Nigerian
OL,13,Fcapital, Abuja, tested positive for the
OL,14,Fvirus on 20 October, becoming the
OL,15,Fcountry's first confirmed Ebola patient
OL,16,Fin more than a decade.
OL,18,FThey both travelled to Uganda earlier
OL,19,Fthis month. Her husband is currently in
OL,20,Fisolation but has not developed any
OL,21,Fsymptoms, according to the Swiss
OL,22,Fforeign ministry.
OL,23,APub: 23-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
